1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Last time on Zombieland Saga, the others woke up and started acting like people again!

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Then it was time for us to start our idol activities.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Or it would have been, but nobody really felt like singing and dancing.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Then there was some drama which made Ai and Junko realize how tough the streets could be for a zombie.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
It was mostly just people getting mad at me.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
But it all turned out okay, because that gave me the courage to step up to the mic and spit some hot fire!

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
And that's how we took our first step to becoming a real idol group!

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Uh, if you can call us that.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Alright! Good morning again to all you lovely ladies!

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Uh, good morning to you! I said good morning to you!

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Don't get in her face! You're gonna freak her out!

12
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Straight to business then.

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Clearly diving into that Saga Castle show prematurely was reckless.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,000
So I'm going to be blunt.

15
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
You girls...

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
We're absolutely wonderful!

17
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
You somehow managed to keep your rotten little secret under wraps,

18
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
all the while playing Hot Potato with a disembodied head!

19
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Now that is team spirit!

20
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Your bodies may fall apart, but your hearts stick together!

21
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Which is why I will now bestow my most enthusiastic clapping upon each one of you!

22
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Feel free to join in and applaud your fellow decaying flesh piles on a successful zombying endeavor!

23
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Nice zombying!

24
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
And another thing!

25
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Suck it up!

26
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Sir?

27
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Girl you gotta be...

28
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Uh huh...

29
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Those raps were neat...

30
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Yeah yeah...

31
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,000
You brought the heat...

32
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Foo!

33
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Uh...

34
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Uh...

35
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Uh...

36
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Yeah...

37
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Don't you dare go getting cocky!

38
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Now that your show is over, you think it's all happy party fun time?

39
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Do not lose sight of our main objective!

40
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Snap those necks back around to what's in front of you!

41
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Just because you're dead doesn't mean you can take your sweet time and relax!

42
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,000
The next task I want you crumbling corpses to tackle is...

43
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
One of these...

44
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Gorilla?

45
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
He couldn't spell it...

46
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Do forgive me, but what is a gorilla performance?

47
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Um...

48
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,000
You put on a show in public and don't tell anyone about it, so it's like a fun surprise type thing!

49
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Oh...

50
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Like testing your sword on a passerby!

51
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Heh...

52
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Wait, but if we do a street concert, won't the police come after us again?

53
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Not to worry!

54
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:38,000
As long as you hide your gross faces with makeup, you'll all just get a slap on the wrist!

55
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Don't be such a wimp, Sakura!

56
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
We can't just let the pigs ruin our rally, right?

57
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
And you won't be able to freestyle your way out of it this time!

58
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:52,000
I'll make sure you're all pretty and cute and perfect the way an idol group should be!

59
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,000
I'll teach you!

60
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
One thing...

61
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Yes, Junko?

62
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
It's just...

63
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,000
I've done plenty of solo concerts, but I've never been part of a group before, so I'm a...

64
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
A loner!

65
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
A loner?

66
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
You're a lonely little loser!

67
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Anyway, the performance will be tomorrow morning in the plaza by Karatsu Station.

68
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Tomorrow?

69
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:18,000
We can't learn a whole song and the choreography with just one practice day!

70
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Guess you're gonna have to pull an all-nighter then!

71
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
I mean, what are you gonna do? Die from lack of sleep?

72
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Ha-ha-ha!

73
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

74
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Woo...

75
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Ha...

76
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
You

77
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:06,449
Damn, I had no idea how much crap you're supposed to memorize when you're an idol.

78
00:05:06,709 --> 00:05:09,329
Yeah, but learning new things is good for you.

79
00:05:10,529 --> 00:05:12,229
What's with the racket, Squirt?

80
00:05:12,669 --> 00:05:13,949
My name's not Squirt.

81
00:05:14,469 --> 00:05:18,509
I'm the shining star of stage and screen, Miss Lily Hoshikawa.

82
00:05:18,849 --> 00:05:19,989
Pain in the ass.

83
00:05:20,469 --> 00:05:21,969
Did you want to say something?

84
00:05:21,969 --> 00:05:25,349
Before we practice, I think we should pick a leader.

85
00:05:26,169 --> 00:05:26,409
Leader?

86
00:05:27,229 --> 00:05:27,549
Yeah!

87
00:05:27,549 --> 00:05:29,769
Somebody's got to be in charge of us.

88
00:05:29,989 --> 00:05:32,749
That way there's always someone to make the tough decisions.

89
00:05:33,449 --> 00:05:38,789
In that case, I think it would be a good idea for one of our more experienced idols to be the...

90
00:05:38,789 --> 00:05:39,769
Out of the question.

91
00:05:49,669 --> 00:05:54,749
I'm the first captain of Dorami, the legendary all-female biker gang from Saga Prefecture.

92
00:05:54,989 --> 00:05:56,849
The name is Saki ni Kaido!

93
00:05:57,549 --> 00:06:01,869
I did a damn good job bossing all those biker chicks around!

94
00:06:02,189 --> 00:06:05,589
So wrangling a bunch of baby dolls like you will be a walk in the park!

95
00:06:06,069 --> 00:06:07,269
I pick me!

96
00:06:07,889 --> 00:06:08,989
Geez, we heard ya.

97
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:11,069
Who wants to fight me for captain?

98
00:06:13,349 --> 00:06:14,889
Looks like it's just you.

99
00:06:15,249 --> 00:06:15,869
Aw, yeah!

100
00:06:15,869 --> 00:06:18,029
We're coming to get you, Japan!

101
00:06:18,029 --> 00:06:19,749
You want to start with Kyushu?

102
00:06:19,749 --> 00:06:21,589
It's leader, not captain.

103
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:23,089
This isn't a biker gang.

104
00:06:23,089 --> 00:06:24,089
Leader!

105
00:06:24,089 --> 00:06:25,589
We need a group name!

106
00:06:25,589 --> 00:06:26,589
Huh?

107
00:06:26,589 --> 00:06:27,589
We don't have one?

108
00:06:27,589 --> 00:06:30,089
You mean like Death Musume and Greenface?

109
00:06:30,089 --> 00:06:33,089
None of Tatsumi's dumb ideas are idly enough!

110
00:06:33,089 --> 00:06:34,629
That's a good point.

111
00:06:34,629 --> 00:06:35,889
How about this one?

112
00:06:35,889 --> 00:06:39,629
We could be magical cutie Lily is a lily ass!

113
00:06:41,129 --> 00:06:42,249
That's a lot of lily.

114
00:06:42,929 --> 00:06:46,009
I'm not gonna spend eternity with a kiddie ass group name like that.

115
00:06:46,009 --> 00:06:48,789
I was thinking something more like this.

116
00:06:50,129 --> 00:06:51,969
Could you read that out loud?

117
00:06:51,969 --> 00:06:53,489
Says Joan of Arc!

118
00:06:54,189 --> 00:06:54,789
Does it?

119
00:06:55,509 --> 00:06:57,629
I think it has a noble ring to it.

120
00:06:57,629 --> 00:06:58,509
You do?

121
00:06:58,509 --> 00:07:00,229
She gets what I'm talking about!

122
00:07:00,649 --> 00:07:02,989
However, perhaps this would serve us.

123
00:07:04,209 --> 00:07:05,309
Amiibu wolves?

124
00:07:05,889 --> 00:07:07,489
Hey, that's pretty awesome!

125
00:07:07,929 --> 00:07:08,629
As if.

126
00:07:09,329 --> 00:07:10,449
They'd visit me.

127
00:07:11,909 --> 00:07:13,409
Back in Shimabara.

128
00:07:13,809 --> 00:07:15,129
Oh, no fair, you guys!

129
00:07:15,189 --> 00:07:16,889
I want to be called something cuter!

130
00:07:17,289 --> 00:07:19,009
I also do need to be cute.

131
00:07:19,669 --> 00:07:21,229
Why, you little...

132
00:07:21,229 --> 00:07:22,109
Hey, Ty?

133
00:07:22,309 --> 00:07:24,329
We're trying to have a conversation here.

134
00:07:35,629 --> 00:07:37,249
Don't put that in your mouth!

135
00:07:37,649 --> 00:07:39,049
It can kill you!

136
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:40,829
For the last time, we're zombies.

137
00:07:40,829 --> 00:07:41,029
Oh, please!

138
00:07:47,029 --> 00:07:47,549
No!

139
00:07:50,549 --> 00:07:52,469
Oh, this is getting ridiculous.

140
00:07:52,989 --> 00:07:54,009
Figure it out, Sakura.

141
00:07:54,869 --> 00:07:55,189
Huh?

142
00:07:55,289 --> 00:07:56,229
But why me?

143
00:07:56,329 --> 00:07:57,629
Because I said so?

144
00:07:58,289 --> 00:07:59,829
Well, let me think here.

145
00:07:59,989 --> 00:08:01,289
Oh, how about Frambois?

146
00:08:01,589 --> 00:08:02,909
Oh, that's really cute!

147
00:08:03,589 --> 00:08:04,789
Frambo-what now?

148
00:08:04,789 --> 00:08:07,549
Oh, that's kind of hard to read.

149
00:08:07,829 --> 00:08:09,829
A badass logo is half the battle.

150
00:08:10,149 --> 00:08:12,289
You took a cute word and made it look stinky.

151
00:08:12,629 --> 00:08:15,889
Well, we are dead, so I'm sure we do have a terrible stench.

152
00:08:15,889 --> 00:08:27,389
Let's get back to that group name.

153
00:08:27,649 --> 00:08:28,149
Any more?

154
00:08:28,589 --> 00:08:30,229
I bet Sakura's got some.

155
00:08:30,869 --> 00:08:31,589
Let's see.

156
00:08:31,849 --> 00:08:33,209
How does French high sound?

157
00:08:33,409 --> 00:08:35,229
Not that, but it should be something French.

158
00:08:35,449 --> 00:08:37,629
French bread, French fries, French toast.

159
00:08:37,829 --> 00:08:39,009
What else is from France?

160
00:08:39,429 --> 00:08:40,289
Cream puffs?

161
00:08:40,349 --> 00:08:40,629
Russ!

162
00:08:40,969 --> 00:08:41,709
Oh, dear.

163
00:08:41,709 --> 00:08:43,509
Ew, she's all inky!

164
00:08:43,989 --> 00:08:45,709
She's sneezing from the marker?

165
00:08:45,789 --> 00:08:46,669
Ah, sissy!

166
00:08:47,289 --> 00:08:48,389
You okay, Tai?

167
00:08:49,989 --> 00:08:51,529
I get it now.

168
00:08:51,949 --> 00:08:52,369
What?

169
00:08:52,569 --> 00:08:54,189
Am I missing something here?

170
00:08:54,749 --> 00:08:57,089
I don't think Tai was just sneezing.

171
00:08:57,689 --> 00:08:58,209
Really?

172
00:08:58,829 --> 00:09:01,369
I mean, she is, but it's more than that.

173
00:09:01,469 --> 00:09:02,029
Ah, sissy!

174
00:09:02,689 --> 00:09:03,289
You see?

175
00:09:03,529 --> 00:09:06,489
We needed a new name, and she picked the perfect one!

176
00:09:07,629 --> 00:09:08,949
From Shushu!

177
00:09:08,949 --> 00:09:11,189
Doesn't it sound so pretty and cool?

178
00:09:11,709 --> 00:09:12,569
From Shushu?

179
00:09:12,869 --> 00:09:14,169
Yeah, you like it?

180
00:09:14,869 --> 00:09:15,949
From Shushu.

181
00:09:16,149 --> 00:09:17,209
From Shushu.

182
00:09:17,749 --> 00:09:21,849
You know, I don't hate it.

183
00:09:22,109 --> 00:09:22,429
Indeed.

184
00:09:22,849 --> 00:09:24,429
It is quite an elegant name.

185
00:09:24,869 --> 00:09:25,989
So cute, right?

186
00:09:26,309 --> 00:09:28,529
It's way better than what he came up with.

187
00:09:28,749 --> 00:09:29,669
From Shushu.

188
00:09:30,349 --> 00:09:32,869
Wow, the more you say it, the more adorable it sounds.

189
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:35,029
You did a great job, Tai.

190
00:09:36,949 --> 00:09:38,449
From Shushu.

191
00:09:39,449 --> 00:09:40,749
Yep, looks good to me.

192
00:09:40,749 --> 00:09:41,749
I'll write it like that.

193
00:09:43,149 --> 00:09:44,189
Have it your way.

194
00:09:44,909 --> 00:09:46,009
All right, it's official.

195
00:09:46,269 --> 00:09:49,429
From now on, the seven of us are going to be called Frans Shushu.

196
00:09:49,769 --> 00:09:52,589
Now we just need to actually learn the song for tomorrow.

197
00:09:53,409 --> 00:09:53,889
Right!

198
00:09:54,549 --> 00:09:55,029
Sweet!

199
00:09:55,289 --> 00:09:56,729
Here we go, Frans Shushu!

200
00:09:56,949 --> 00:09:59,549
It's time to practice till our butts fall off!

201
00:09:59,909 --> 00:10:00,449
You ready?

202
00:10:00,449 --> 00:10:00,849
Hey!

203
00:10:01,689 --> 00:10:02,169
Yeah!

204
00:10:02,169 --> 00:10:02,529
Yeah!

205
00:10:05,529 --> 00:10:07,409
I don't think we can do this.

206
00:10:07,909 --> 00:10:09,369
It's way too hard.

207
00:10:10,009 --> 00:10:14,749
I thought I was starting to understand, but singing and dancing are way tougher than I thought.

208
00:10:14,749 --> 00:10:18,489
If we blow it, we're done for.

209
00:10:18,529 --> 00:10:20,089
There's just not enough time.

210
00:10:20,189 --> 00:10:22,909
I and Junko are the only ones who know what they're doing.

211
00:10:25,909 --> 00:10:26,389
Tai?

212
00:10:26,549 --> 00:10:31,149
We haven't even pulled it off once during practice, and tomorrow we'll have an audience.

213
00:10:31,149 --> 00:10:34,969
We're about to get thrown off.

214
00:10:35,469 --> 00:10:36,609
I don't want to!

215
00:10:37,609 --> 00:10:39,529
I should have thought about this logically.

216
00:10:40,149 --> 00:10:42,709
Being zombies is crazy enough, but zombie idols?

217
00:10:44,809 --> 00:10:45,249
Frans Shushu!

218
00:10:45,249 --> 00:10:47,009
Get off that thing now!

219
00:10:47,109 --> 00:10:49,229
Still though, I have to see this through.

220
00:10:49,809 --> 00:10:54,489
I want to relive that feeling I had the first time I was on stage, and figure out what it was.

221
00:10:54,489 --> 00:10:57,489
Frans Shushu!

222
00:11:10,249 --> 00:11:10,729
Sakura!

223
00:11:11,269 --> 00:11:12,229
Are you okay?

224
00:11:15,169 --> 00:11:18,469
I'm going back in, so I can practice some more.

225
00:11:18,589 --> 00:11:18,989
Whoa.

226
00:11:19,129 --> 00:11:23,049
Saki, Lily, Tai, even though we're zombies now,

227
00:11:23,049 --> 00:11:25,369
as long as everybody works hard.

228
00:11:26,929 --> 00:11:29,509
I know we have a chance to achieve our-

229
00:11:29,509 --> 00:11:39,409
Shame on you!

230
00:11:40,049 --> 00:11:41,389
Whatever happened to practicing?

231
00:11:42,109 --> 00:11:44,369
I'm confident that even though we're zombies now,

232
00:11:44,909 --> 00:11:48,889
if we work hard, it'll be possible for us to achieve our mission.

233
00:11:48,889 --> 00:11:53,169
Um, that's what I was about to-

234
00:11:53,169 --> 00:11:54,029
Yugiri's right.

235
00:11:54,189 --> 00:11:55,449
We don't need your negativity.

236
00:11:56,149 --> 00:11:57,349
But-

237
00:11:57,349 --> 00:12:00,249
Yeah, she knew just what to say to get us all motivated!

238
00:12:00,949 --> 00:12:01,349
Hmph.

239
00:12:03,269 --> 00:12:03,749
Cool.

240
00:12:04,829 --> 00:12:06,069
They've been gone a while.

241
00:12:06,769 --> 00:12:07,109
Hmm.

242
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:10,609
Yugiri was supposed to bring the girls back here.

243
00:12:11,509 --> 00:12:12,909
Do you think they gave up?

244
00:12:12,909 --> 00:12:17,929
I think it might be better if they did.

245
00:12:18,929 --> 00:12:22,009
You can't pull off an idle performance overnight.

246
00:12:23,009 --> 00:12:25,769
Besides, if the show doesn't go well,

247
00:12:26,129 --> 00:12:28,169
then the audience won't have a good time.

248
00:12:29,449 --> 00:12:32,829
If it's from the heart, they'll still appreciate it.

249
00:12:32,829 --> 00:12:37,809
But that's if.

250
00:12:38,989 --> 00:12:41,009
All right, let's get crackin'!

251
00:12:41,009 --> 00:12:44,329
We're gonna put on a damn good show tomorrow!

252
00:12:45,329 --> 00:12:45,689
Yeah!

253
00:12:45,689 --> 00:12:54,969
One, two, three, four.

254
00:12:55,289 --> 00:12:56,729
One, two, three, and four.

255
00:12:56,829 --> 00:12:58,349
And one, two, three, four.

256
00:12:58,629 --> 00:12:59,949
One, two, three, four.

257
00:13:00,249 --> 00:13:01,689
One, two, three, four.

258
00:13:01,909 --> 00:13:02,569
One, two.

259
00:13:02,729 --> 00:13:03,409
Oh, Lily!

260
00:13:03,809 --> 00:13:04,749
Are you hurt?

261
00:13:04,949 --> 00:13:07,009
The steps for this part are so tricky.

262
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:08,849
Then try dancin' better.

263
00:13:09,069 --> 00:13:10,289
Wow, thanks for the tip!

264
00:13:10,389 --> 00:13:12,149
Stop bickering, both of you!

265
00:13:12,149 --> 00:13:22,709
Sorry.

266
00:13:27,109 --> 00:13:30,969
Well, I think we should keep practisin' with or without him.

267
